# `npm run dev:live` — the SPA against a real API, instead of fixtures.
#
# Loaded by vite only in `--mode live`, which is what `dev:live` passes. Plain `npm run dev` runs
# in mode `development`, never reads this file, and keeps answering from `src/fixtures` — which is
# the correct default and the one `vitest --project web` depends on.
#
# Tracked, and it holds no secret. `VITE_API_LIVE` is a **boolean**, not an address: fixtures
# versus live is a property of the build, and the api's address is the page's own origin, carried
# there by the dev server's `/api` proxy. See `vite.config.ts` for where that proxy points (the
# dev api on 3083) and `src/gateway/index.ts` for why there is no URL here to get wrong.
#
# It is a separate mode rather than a variable you export because Windows has no `VAR=x cmd`
# prefix, so a shell-specific incantation in package.json would work in Git Bash and fail in
# PowerShell — and this repository is used from both.
VITE_API_LIVE=true
